    "alert_id": "P003_EFV_NEUROPSYCH_001",
    "title": "EFV neuropsychiatric toxicity causing insomnia and vivid dreams",
    "message": "Guidelines state EFV frequently causes neuropsychiatric effects including insomnia, vivid dreams, and dizziness, typically within the first 2-6 weeks of therapy. This patient started EFV in February 2024 and now reports poor sleep and vivid dreams for several weeks. Evidence for drug attribution: symptoms match the classic EFV neuropsychiatric profile. Evidence against: onset is unusually late (nearly 2 years after initiation), so other causes such as anxiety, depression, or substance use should be excluded. The guideline lists persistent CNS toxicity or mental symptoms as a major adverse event warranting regimen substitution.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Assess for alternative causes; if symptoms persist or are intolerable, substitute EFV per guideline (e.g., switch to an alternative third agent).",
